$|H|_{dB} = -10\log_{10}\left(1 + (f_1/f_B)^2\right) = -{{X}}$ dB gives $(f_1/f_B)^2 = 10^{ {{X}}/10 } - 1$ = {{10^(X/10) - 1}}, so
$f_B = \frac{f_1}{\sqrt{10^{X/10} - 1}}$ = {{f1|Hz}} / {{sqrt(10^(X/10) - 1)||3}} = {{fBt|Hz}}
$C = \frac{1}{2\pi Rf_B}$ = 1 / (2π × {{R|Ω}} × {{fBt|Hz}}) = **{{Ct|F}}**. (3 dB attenuation means $f_B = f_1$; far above $f_B$ every extra 20 dB needs one more decade.)
